
Linux is a free, open-source operating system kernel that serves as the foundation for many complete operating systems called Linux distributions (or "distros"). It was created in 1991 by Linus Torvalds.



Think of it this way:
====================
Kernel: The core software that manages your computer's hardware (CPU, memory, storage, devices).
Operating system: The kernel plus tools, libraries, desktop environments, and applications that make a usable system.



Popular Linux distributions include:
====================================
Ubuntu – beginner-friendly and widely used.
Fedora Project – features newer software and is popular with developers.
Debian Project – known for stability.
Arch Linux – highly customizable for advanced users.
Linux Mint – designed to be easy for people switching from Windows.



Why people use Linux
====================
Free and open source:        Anyone can inspect, modify, and distribute the source code.
Secure:                      Strong permissions and a large open-source community help identify and fix issues.
Stable:                      Many servers run Linux because it can operate reliably for long periods.
Customizable:                You can choose different desktop environments, software, and system configurations.
Efficient:                   It can run well on both modern and older hardware.



Linux vs. Windows vs. macOS
===========================
| Feature       | Linux                      | Windows                       | macOS                                 |
| ------------- | -------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Cost          | Usually free               | Paid license                  | Included with Apple hardware          |
| Source code   | Open source                | Proprietary                   | Mostly proprietary                    |
| Customization | Very high                  | Moderate                      | Limited                               |
| Software      | Huge open-source ecosystem | Excellent commercial software | Strong creative and productivity apps |
| Gaming        | Improving rapidly          | Best overall support          | Limited compared to Windows           |

